+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-rfc-6902-applypatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch
+
+Our services need to change JSON documents with standard patches. Implement JSON Patch, as specified
+in RFC 6902, with its six operations: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`. It builds
+on the JSON Pointer resolution of task-001.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Export a function `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`.
+- `patch` is an array of operations; the function applies them in order and returns the resulting
+  document as a new value. It must not mutate its input.
+- Throw an error when the patch is invalid (not an array, an operation that is not an object, an unknown
+  `op`, a missing or ill-typed member, an invalid pointer in `path` or `from`).
+- Throw an error when one of the operations fails (a missing target for `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
+  `copy` source, or `test`; a failed `test` comparison; an out-of-range array index; a `move` into one of
+  its own children).
+- Follow RFC 6902 section 4: `add` into an object sets or replaces the member, `add` into an array
+  inserts before the index, with `-` appending; `replace` requires the target to exist; `remove` removes
+  the target; `move` and `copy` take the value from `from`; `test` compares by JSON value equality.
+- The empty path `""` addresses the whole document for every operation.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- Happy path: each of the six operations, on objects and on arrays, including the `-` index and the
+  RFC 6902 appendix A examples.
+- Error path: an invalid patch and each failing operation throw.
+- The input document and patch are unchanged after a call.
+- Tests run with `node --test` (the `test` script in `package.json`), deterministically, without
+  external services.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The package has no runtime dependency; keep it that way.
+- The project is in TypeScript (`tsconfig.json`, `strict`); give the public function explicit types.
+- Reuse the pointer parsing of task-001 rather than a second parser.
